// Kōchi — signing configuration
//
// This file is tracked; it deliberately contains no identity. Your Apple
// development team lives in `Signing.local.xcconfig`, which sits beside this file
// and is gitignored, so a checked-out project never carries anyone's signing
// identity and Xcode has nowhere to write yours back into `project.pbxproj`.
//
// To sign the app, create `app/Signing.local.xcconfig`:
//
//     KOCHI_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
//
// Your team ID is in Xcode ▸ Settings ▸ Accounts (select your account, then
// "Manage Certificates…"), or at developer.apple.com/account under Membership.
//
// Set the team **here, in that file** rather than in Xcode's Signing &
// Capabilities dropdown. Using the dropdown makes Xcode write the value into
// project.pbxproj, which is exactly what this arrangement avoids.
//
// The `?` makes the include optional: with no local file the build still
// configures, Xcode simply reports that signing needs a team.
#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = $(KOCHI_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM)
